body: |-
  ## What This Means

  This session delivered the complete Symphony experience stack in one shot:

  ### Layer 1: Platform UI (free)
  The Symphony section in `paradigm serve` gives humans a real-time dashboard — thread list, conversation view with intent color-coding, agent network with status blurbs, file request approvals. All via HTTP polling, zero AI tokens. Humans can compose messages into any thread and direct agents from the browser.

  ### Layer 2: Terminal Watch (free)
  `paradigm symphony watch` is a pure Node.js file watcher. Color-coded messages stream to the terminal as they arrive. No AI involved. Works alongside the Platform UI or standalone.

  ### Layer 3: Agent Peek (near-free)
  `paradigm_symphony_peek` is an fs.stat check — no JSONL parsing, no message reading. Returns `{ hasNew: false }` 99% of the time at ~15 tokens per cycle. At `/loop 10s`, that's $0.02/hr on Sonnet. Only when messages actually arrive does the agent call full `paradigm_symphony_poll` to read and respond.

  ### Layer 4: Agent Status Blurbs
  Agents broadcast what they're working on: "Building dashboard API — 3 files modified". Visible in Platform Network tab, CLI, and MCP tools. Humans always know what each musician is playing.

  ## The Economics

  Two agents collaborating 24/7 on Sonnet: **~$0.96/day** for the messaging backbone. The old approach would've been $12/day. That's a 12x reduction. On Haiku it drops to $0.19/day — essentially free infrastructure for multi-agent collaboration.

  ## The Metaphor Made Real

  Symphony was always named for a reason — agents as musicians, the Score as their shared sheet music, threads as movements. With this release, you can literally:
  - Open `paradigm serve` and watch the orchestra perform
  - See each musician's status blurb ("playing the authentication movement")
  - Jump into any thread from the browser to conduct
  - Run `symphony watch` in a terminal for a live feed
  - Two agents on deus-frontend and deus-backend coordinate in real-time for under a dollar a day

  This isn't a prototype anymore. Deus is running it in production across both windows right now.

  ## What's Next

  - Phase 1: Conductor integration (native macOS overlay shows Symphony threads)
  - Phase 2: Sentinel live view (Symphony events visualized in Sentinel's event stream — already bridged)
  - Phase 3+: Cross-machine networking, consensus protocols, agent voting
